{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761969-need-help-with-challenge-between-two-garou","id":761969,"title":"need help with challenge between two garou","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-09T20:19:12-08:00","id":761969,"title":"need help with challenge between two garou","content":"I need some help on how to handle disputes between Garou that get out of hand, but aren't that serious. This is not a challenge for rank, but simple dispute.<br /> <br /> Two Garou of equal rank get into a dispute. One insulted the other, but was overheard. The offended party takes a swing at him, but the fight is stopped before it escalates. The one challenges the other.<br /> <br /> What would be an appropriate contest/challenge to resolve? Presumably, this is like a duel fought to defend one's honor. What is the equivalent duel to restore the offended party's pride? This isn't something that should degenerate into serious fighting. I think it should be more than just a Staredown, but something less than lethal fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T20:22:16-08:00","id":761971,"title":"","content":"Well tribe, breed and auspice factor in here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T20:46:04-08:00","id":761980,"title":"","content":"Without more information, I've seen disputes like this generally settled with combat using bashing or lethal weapons. Usually in a form that can regenerate.<br /> The combat should be far from fatal for either of the Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T22:30:12-08:00","id":762014,"title":"","content":"anything from a brawl to a rap battle. i personally go with rap battles, but thats mostly because its funny to see my players rap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T22:33:07-08:00","id":762015,"title":"","content":"A duel to first blood is pretty generic, which is appropriate given the lack of details. If the insult was an alleged inadequacy of oral talent lodged by one Glass Walker Galliard against another, try roleplaying a rap battle. That would be entertaining.<br /> <br /> Edit: Damn, Nasrudin ninjaed my idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T02:00:11-08:00","id":762103,"title":"","content":"A grievance challenge. <br /> <br /> I believe it's usually down to the Garou that was challenged to pick the type of challenge (wisdom, glory or honor i usually go by. For a quick Greviance challenge i make it Glory unless the challenger directly tests their honor or wisdom) and then down to the Master of Challenge to oversee it is as fair a contest as possible. Then declare the winner.<br /> <br /> First blood is good, but then you get the character who cuts themselves to win by drawing 'first blood' so be sure to declare first blood upon your competitor unless you want to intentionally leave it vague.<br /> <br /> I do knock outs. As in first one to get knocked down and out. Or three turns of attacks and then measure who has taken the least injuries to be the victor.<br /> <br /> Challenges like this can be so many things. I'd take the Sept and feel of the tribe in charge into reflecting how challenges are done too. It should also be noted there's nothing wrong with settling things by challenges. It is in fact the right way to do it in garou society. No shame in losing either, you stood true to yourself among friends and peers and had the courage to stand and compete for your convictions.<br /> <br /> I only add that last bit as I've seen a lot of players get bent out of shape over just being challenged and fearing what a loss may incur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T02:43:22-08:00","id":762133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761969-need-help-with-challenge-between-two-garou?p=762103#post762103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Challenges like this can be so many things. I'd take the Sept and feel of the tribe in charge into reflecting how challenges are done too. It should also be noted there's nothing wrong with settling things by challenges. It is in fact the right way to do it in garou society. No shame in losing either, you stood true to yourself among friends and peers and had the courage to stand and compete for your convictions.<br /> <br /> I only add that last bit as I've seen a lot of players get bent out of shape over just being challenged and fearing what a loss may incur.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a sadly common thing, yeah. Losing as a shame is a thing that really needs to be disproven. Unless is a challenge of ones honour, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T03:11:52-08:00","id":762140,"title":"","content":"The nature of the grievance is a possible factor if the challenge is not combat oriented.<br /> <br /> Outside this I find first blood to be not that good a system, as the rules factor in luck (dice rules) in addition to skill and that probably isn't satisfying. Lethal damage might also lead to Battle Scars, therefore it might be suitable (if the combatants are meant to really wager with their health) but not suitable in all cases.<br /> So, the seriousness of the challenge plays a part in choosing the means of resolution.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T03:28:04-08:00","id":762145,"title":"","content":"Can we have some background, on what exactly led to the challenge?<br /> More often than not, the challenge mirrors the offence in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T05:50:49-08:00","id":762226,"title":"","content":"Scars are gloriously awesome. But probably better to get them from fighting the wyrm rather than each other in a grudge grievance match. <br /> <br /> Anything that adds drama or highlights the garous abilities and strengths and durability can only be a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T06:25:16-08:00","id":762250,"title":"","content":"Scars aren't all equal.<br /> A Battle Scar from a huge battle is a glorious thing, but also makes you a gimp. But if you can tell the story you deserve renown.<br /> If the story is, that you slipped while balancing on a high ledge to impress a girl an fell down 12 floors, so rules dictate you get a Battle Scar - well less glorious. Even worst when you have to admit that you were to stupid to handle your own gun and shot yourself.<br /> <br /> That is totally opposed to the Scars made permanent with the Rite of Wounding, that can be Battle Scars but could be other wounds from the battle as well...<br /> Those are only done if the battle was glorious...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T06:47:10-08:00","id":762267,"title":"","content":"Exactly why I said &quot;better to get them from fighting the wyrm&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T06:58:43-08:00","id":762272,"title":"","content":"True, just wanted to contradict &quot;Scars are gloriously awesome.&quot; a little - for Werewolf certainly promotes such a stance, but with the inadequacies of the combat system battle scars seemed to be something STs should omit to not have their player characters handicapped after trainings battles. Especially in 2nd Edition, when there wasn't bashing damage and when battle scars were rolled, instead of chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T07:25:37-08:00","id":762288,"title":"","content":"No garou lives for ever though. In the end the only thing they'll be remembered for was for how awesome they were and the daring deeds of glory honor and wisdom they performed. Sure a battle scar might hinder, but that also means the garou could be more ferocious and brave to get the fight over. Or more cowardly and let everyone do the hard work and take the first hits for them so they survive longer. But what gatou would want to live longer in cowardice?<br /> <br /> Just food for thought. Sorry for the derailment. <br /> <br /> I'm all for not making the garou look weak and careful of not getting booboos. <br /> <br /> But I fully recommend in challenges like this a little blood and endurance. Fists wrapped in barbed wire for bonegnawers. Train jumping for Glasswalkers. Arm wrestling for Get of Fenris with candles or red hot branding irons for the loser to get their hand pressed too. Archery for Blackfuries where spectators do what they can to distract or unbalance the shot fired bewteen both competitors. Wendigo tests of bravery involving a small circle they cannot leave while opponents throw spears at each other. The loser is the one who leaves the circle or can no longer throw due to injuries. Uktena summoning spirits, the one with the most powerful and respectdd at the end wins. There's so many options that dont have to involve aggravated damage and victory doesnt need to come from incapitating the opponent, just beating them at the end of a few rounds and a narrow margin is enough.<br /> <br /> Drama, flavour, strength and add fire or sharp objects for personal touches is my recipe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T07:56:10-08:00","id":762313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761969-need-help-with-challenge-between-two-garou#post761969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The offended party takes a swing at him, but the fight is stopped before it escalates. The one challenges the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the one frenzied, it sounds like the challenge had started and somebody interrupted it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T08:23:40-08:00","id":762337,"title":"","content":"While I agree with Somuchlove on the principal way of the Challenges, I think that garou aren't reckless in their use of &quot;toughness&quot;. Meaning that in game mechanic terms, they won't suffer damage 'til Incapacitated. Possibly the challenge is within game mechanic terms rigged to only inflict one increment of health per failure on the contestants part (or success on the opponents part).<br /> <br /> Leaving all the &quot;toughness&quot; to the Storytelling and fluff, and keeping the stakes of the challenge with renown loss or gain - as opposed to character death or crippledness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T08:32:37-08:00","id":762340,"title":"","content":"The only challenge that should be to the death is 'challenges to the death'. Breaking the terms of the challenge and being reckless could be seen as dishonorable and unwise. Immobolisation, pinning the throat, knock out, crippled, garou heal and have kinfolk and packmstes to tend to them as they do so. Plus if you're feeling really generous a Theurge with mothers touch can come in handy.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm for Drama. I dont think kitten gloves and bashing damage quite have the same dramatic effect. Unless the kitten gloves are on fire. <br /> <br /> But it's your game, do it how ever you want too, as long as the players have fun that's what counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T14:37:37-08:00","id":762605,"title":"","content":"Older novels and books had duels banned by sept elders, due to the high amount of accidental deaths. Besides the frenzy risk there is the danger that you land a killing blow simply be rolling good and/or the opponent not scoring well on soak. If not bashing, Incapacitated means a Battle Scar but also could mean death if not tended to. If the Incapacitated garou uses &quot;remain active&quot; he frenzies and now the fight is lethal, probably even for spectators.<br /> If, because it serves the mood, the duel was Fangs and Claws, the damage is aggravated in any case, with means most likely death if Incapacitated and remains active fails. And even if a healer jumps in and tries to use magic, the roll may fail.<br /> <br /> Basically the combat system is the weak spot, imo. If damage was aggravated but limited to some degree, the fight could be prolonged, there was drama, but also characters would have the ability to actually surrender in a meaningful way. All to often I see garou who fight proud, having lost three health, and would surrender if they had lost five or six, but don't have the chance because they are incapacitated in a single strike. That is not that good story wise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T15:35:25-08:00","id":762659,"title":"","content":"I say challenge by dance-off! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T20:17:57-08:00","id":762786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761969-need-help-with-challenge-between-two-garou?p=761971#post761971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well tribe, breed and auspice factor in here</div> </div> </div> </div>Get of Fenris and Silver Fang in a traditional, but multi-tribal sept. The two tribes are dominant here. Fenrir Ragabash was making fun of some recent actions by the Silver Fang's pack in &quot;private&quot; conversation that the Silver Fang realized was meant to be overheard. Silver Fang Theurge came into area, acted like he didn't hear, and when he got close enough took a surprise swing at him. Ragabash went to attack him back, but was held back by third party who said to do a formal challenge.<br /> <br /> The Theurge was the one originally offended, but I think it is in the Ragabash's court since the attack was a suprise. Both will likely claim they are the offended party. Both will want &quot;honor&quot; done to them.<br /> <br /> It's mainly my attempt to show players how these things are handled by the Garou. Both PC (SF) and NPC (GF) are Cliath.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T20:19:03-08:00","id":762787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761969-need-help-with-challenge-between-two-garou?p=762313#post762313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the one frenzied, it sounds like the challenge had started and somebody interrupted it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correct. An elder character stepped to prevent it from being a mindless brawl so the two Cliath can learn to handle these things &quot;right&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T20:37:49-08:00","id":762799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761969-need-help-with-challenge-between-two-garou?p=762786#post762786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Get of Fenris and Silver Fang in a traditional, but multi-tribal sept. The two tribes are dominant here. Fenrir Ragabash was making fun of some recent actions by the Silver Fang's pack in &quot;private&quot; conversation that the Silver Fang realized was meant to be overheard. Silver Fang Theurge came into area, acted like he didn't hear, and when he got close enough took a surprise swing at him. Ragabash went to attack him back, but was held back by third party who said to do a formal challenge.<br /> <br /> The Theurge was the one originally offended, but I think it is in the Ragabash's court since the attack was a suprise. Both will likely claim they are the offended party. Both will want &quot;honor&quot; done to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who was the third party that broke it up?<br /> The Silver Fang certainly sounds like they were the one to act dishonorably (taking a surprise swing). Given that, and the expectation of Get (even Ragabash) to favor physical challenges, a non lethal fight would be easy enough to settle it in my opinion.<br /> System-wise there are at least a few options. If it's being taken to the Master of Challenges (Which is what Tribe/Aupsice/Breed?) then the risk of frenzy could be mitigated, depending on gifts available. That would allow for lethal weapons to be used in the challenge with less risk. Otherwise, a fight using brawl or weapons that deal bashing damage would work out fine with the loser being the one that is beaten unconscious.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761969-need-help-with-challenge-between-two-garou?p=762786#post762786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mainly my attempt to show players how these things are handled by the Garou. Both PC (SF) and NPC (GF) are Cliath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've generally shown Garou society to be fairly brutal. Garou are tough/resilient enough that being beaten (or stabbed) can be used as simple punishments for little things when cubs and cliaths are being taught.<br /> I've been in a pack where the Ragabash has been held down to have his arm broken (a few times) for stealing a trinket from another pack member. He had insisted it was a prank, but the pack was not amused). Garou heal and there was no lasting damage but the lesson was learned.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T20:42:59-08:00","id":762803,"title":"","content":"Well since both tribes involved are the dominant ones at the sept I would imagine elders would want to get involved for political reasons.<br /> <br /> When I say involved I mean in more of a observer position as the outcome gives each side some political &quot;hay&quot; so to speak, it could even gain the PC a mentor or at least a stern talking to by an elder silver fang over such &quot;un kingly&quot; behavior.<br /> <br /> Since both tribes are the more marital bent I would suggest a simple wrestling match in a circle. Winner was right and the loser has to fetch and step for a lunar phase sorta thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 11-10-2015, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T19:45:28-08:00","id":763686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761969-need-help-with-challenge-between-two-garou?p=762803#post762803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since both tribes are the more marital bent I would suggest a simple wrestling match in a circle. Winner was right and the loser has to fetch and step for a lunar phase sorta thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. The result of the challenge is ultimately unimportant, but it produces a real (if petty) stake as losing will be galling.<br /> <br /> The dispute will be brought up at the next Moot during the Cracking of the Bone. Is that when the actual challenge should be done? Or after the moot (say the next night)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T19:53:47-08:00","id":763694,"title":"","content":"Well really it's your call if it's moot worthy, imo it isn't but if the elders want it to be then yes. <br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the offended garou would call out the other after the cracking of the bone and then the master of the challenge would lay out the terms and referee the match then and there if the elders want it settled. Plus it provides the loser the fetching and stepping at the revel afterwards.<br /> <br /> Edit: now that I've thought about it the Get are known to have a bit of a brawl to kick off moots (gets the blood going both spiritually and physically) so the two settling the dispute could be the opening event. To the silver fangs it's settling a matter of honor and to the Get it's glorious combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Had a beer thought of something better 11-11-2015, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T08:22:09-08:00","id":764073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761969-need-help-with-challenge-between-two-garou?p=762786#post762786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Get of Fenris and Silver Fang in a traditional, but multi-tribal sept. The two tribes are dominant here. Fenrir Ragabash was making fun of some recent actions by the Silver Fang's pack in &quot;private&quot; conversation that the Silver Fang realized was meant to be overheard. Silver Fang Theurge came into area, acted like he didn't hear, and when he got close enough took a surprise swing at him. Ragabash went to attack him back, but was held back by third party who said to do a formal challenge.<br /> <br /> The Theurge was the one originally offended, but I think it is in the Ragabash's court since the attack was a suprise. Both will likely claim they are the offended party. Both will want &quot;honor&quot; done to them.<br /> <br /> It's mainly my attempt to show players how these things are handled by the Garou. Both PC (SF) and NPC (GF) are Cliath.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on who the Master of the Challenge like more of course, but have you considered that both parties acted dishonorably? The RAgabash is supposed to do constructive criticism to one's face, not backtalking, and the Theurge should not have taken a surprise swing like that.<br /> I'd say the Master of the Challenge should slap them both and tell them to quit the bullshit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}